From 13e81b9ab02de07777bec74a5b239a30b15745c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Koehler-Killeen <kohlykohl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 03:28:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gx: stop the detached decoder and interpolation helper
 threads on shutdown

Two detached background threads never terminated and hung the process
at exit():

- texture_replacement.cpp's decoder_main() waited on s_decodeCv forever,
  with no stop signal.
- gxcore_draw.cpp's interp_helper_main() waited on the helper's work
  condition variable forever (the helper was intentionally never
  destroyed).

glibc's exit() teardown then hung waiting on the still-live detached
threads. Add a stop flag to each, check it in the wait predicate, and
signal it from texture_replacement::shutdown() and gxcore::shutdown() so
both threads exit before process teardown.
---
 .../graphics/aurora/lib/gfx/gxcore_draw.cpp   | 20 ++++++++++++++++++-
 .../aurora/lib/gfx/texture_replacement.cpp    | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/GXRuntime/graphics/aurora/lib/gfx/gxcore_draw.cpp b/GXRuntime/graphics/aurora/lib/gfx/gxcore_draw.cpp
